The Go rendering: a command that steps through two enumerated types by an
increment loop up to a named last member (one type with a String method, one
without), a third and a fourth whose values come from a compound assignment and a
binary expression and whose later members nothing names, a fifth whose only
arithmetic is on constants, and a sixth type whose middle member only a test
steps through.

